WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.901
-While you're young,
you don't know anything, really,

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:05.701
whereas it is my responsibility
to only grant the wishes

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.868
I am sure are good for Rosas.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.968
♪♪

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:13.968
-So most of these wishes
will never be granted?

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:17.501
-Yet I still protect them
like all the others.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.868
-Can't you just
give them back instead?

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:20.968
-Excuse me?

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.400
-The wishes
you're not going to grant.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.467
You could just give them back.
Then -- I don't know.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:28.934
The people can try
to pursue them themselves?

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:31.167
-We're back with Ariana DeBose,
everybody.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
That was a clip from "Wish."

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:35.200
It's a new Disney movie.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.467
-Yeah, it is.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.033
Celebrating 100 years of Disney.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.334
-100 years. So, this cannot
come soon enough for me.

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:41.734
I mean that sincerely.
-Yeah?

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.634
-Because my boys,
the two older ones,

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.634
they're old enough
to go to movies now.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.901
Bringing them to the movies is
my favorite thing in the world.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.300
And not all kids movies
are good.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:55.200
-Well, I think this one is.
-I believe it is.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.467
I mean, again, it is obviously
in the safe hands of Disney.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.634
And so what was your mom's
reaction when you told her

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.200
you were going to be
in a Disney movie?

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.968
-Oh, she --
I believe it went like this.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.834
"You're doing what?

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.400
Wow! That's big!"

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.467
-Oh, wow.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.167
-I was like,
"Yeah, it's cool, Mom."

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.133
She's like, "No, it's cool.
But this is big.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:15.834
That's like the House of Mouse."

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.400
-That's very --

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.067
I like when your parents
outside of show business

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:21.734
want to let you know
how big something is.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.801
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:26.400
It was a great moment.
We've had many great moments.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.634
-So, tell us a little bit about
your character and the film.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.334
Do not spoil anything
because I'm going to see it.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.167
-I promise I will not.
-Okay. Thank you.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.300
-But I do voice
the character of Asha.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.067
-Great.
-And she's so beautiful.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.901
Beautiful brown skin,
braids, and freckles.

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:40.334
Come on, now.
-Alright.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Um, and...

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.901
And she lives in
the magical kingdom of Rosas.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:48.501
And she is so
community-oriented.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.667
She literally
just loves this space

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:54.801
where she believes
wishes can come true.

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:58.601
And she has this encounter
with King Magnifico

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:01.767
and discovers that things
are not all that they seem.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.467
And she makes a powerful wish

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:08.534
and kind of accidentally
calls down the Wishing Star.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:11.267
And they go on this
really cool journey

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:14.067
of trying to save their --
the community

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:18.567
and make life and the place
that they live better,

00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:20.767
which I think
is kind of indicative

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:23.300
of the world we live in today.
-That's very nice.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.067
It's very nice,
but it's a solid message

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:27.200
for the kids and the adults
who are with the kids.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.667
You got to sing one of the songs
at Disneyland.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.467
-I did. I did.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:34.033
So "This Wish" is what I think

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:37.934
is kind of, like, the mother
of all "I want" songs.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.834
Like, the Disney "I want" songs.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.901
You know, like "Go the Distance"
from "Hercules,"

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:44.067
that sort of thing.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.467
-And I sang it recently

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:49.567
at Aurora's Castle
at Disneyland.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:50.667
I'd never been.

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:52.567
So, cool, cool.
Everything's fine.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:56.868
And it was -- it was so special
for many reasons,

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.734
but mostly because I looked out,

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:02.934
and the kids in the audience
were already singing the song.

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:03.968
-That's a trip.
-You know?

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:05.434
Like, that was --

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:07.334
It was one of those pinch-me
moments when you realize,

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.834
"Oh, this thing
that I said yes to

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:12.067
that I, you know,
had so much fun making..."

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:15.767
I put a lot of heart into it.

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:20.334
And to see that it's being
received from kids already

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:23.400
and that they're going to
sing this beautiful music

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.033
and learn from it
is kind of everything.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:28.000
-That's so lovely.
And it just makes me...

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:33.534
-It also -- It also
just makes me dread

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:36.133
my kids butchering it
in the back seat of the car.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:39.033
-That's -- See, but I like that.
-You like the butchering?

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:40.834
-I'm okay -- Well, come on.
How many songs --

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.000
I mean, "Let It Go."

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.267
♪ Let it go, let it go ♪

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.133
Like, it happens, but...
-Yeah.

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:49.067
-But it makes you
feel good inside.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.734
Like, singing in the shower.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:53.200
♪ So I'll make this wish ♪

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.400
Like, it's fine. Like,
sing to your heart's desire.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.534
-That is still so much better
than them.

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:01.667
[ Laughter ]
Like, that's very cruel

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.667
that you're like,
"Bad like this."

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:05.067
I'm like, "Is that bad, though?"

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:07.534
'Cause I -- I feel like
I would listen to that.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:08.934
-Oh, no.
-What were your favorites?

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:11.100
What was your favorites
growing up, your Disney movies?

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.868
-Oh, I had so many. I --
"Beauty and the Beast."

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.267
I was Belle for Halloween.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.501
I was Snow White
for Halloween.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:20.400
Granted, I'm giving
Evil Queen vibes today.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.601
Anyone?
-Yeah, it's very good.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:24.100
-And honestly,
she was very scary.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.968
"Mulan."
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.801
Like, come on. So graceful.
Everything.

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:33.901
"Hercules." The Muses.
Like, what?!

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.067
There are so many.

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:37.133
But wait. You were a Disney kid.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:38.701
-I grew up with Disney. Yeah.
-So what are your favorites?

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:42.200
-From, like, a different era.
-That's okay.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.067
-"Fantasia." No. Um...

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.234
[ Laughter ]
-Let's take it all the way back.

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:48.434
-These are the ones
that are, like, when I was --

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:51.000
This dates me, but it's always
the ones I saw in the theater.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.534
So "Jungle Book."
"Sword in the Stone."

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.267
"Robin Hood" is one
I really like.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:56.901
"The Rescuers"
was a big one for me.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.133
-Oh, I love "The Rescuers"!
Medusa?!

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.367
-Yeah. Really good.
Really good villain.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.767
-Really great villain.
Were you into "Tarzan"?

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.300
Because I was into "Tarzan."
-I did enjoy --

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.667
-I feel like I maybe --
You know what?

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.300
I'm gonna be honest.
I think I missed "Tarzan."

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.634
-What? Phil Collins?
"Trashin' the Camp"?

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:11.901
-Yeah.
-What?!

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:13.934
-I think, though,
there's this time in your life

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:16.634
between when you're a kid
and when you have them

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:17.968
that you're not like,

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:19.534
"I got to see
the new Disney movie."

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:20.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:22.334
-You know,
I don't have children,

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.567
so I'm gonna say
that that's really fair.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.000
-Yeah. But I will say --
You know what?

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.300
The one that I missed and then
my kids found is "Moana."

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.968
-So good.
-"Moana" now -- I can't --

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.868
And I've seen it a bunch
because it's their favorite.

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:36.067
You know what's interesting?

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:39.200
My oldest says this about
"Moana," and he's a boy.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.834
He's like,
"'Moana' is my favorite

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:43.868
because the girl never
talks about true love."

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:45.033
And I'm like, "Look at them."

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:46.434
And I'm like --
That's really good that

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:48.467
it's, like, not -- like,
there's a female character

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.033
who's just, like, a hero

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:52.100
and it's not about her
trying to, like, find a dude.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.234
-Find love.
And, you know, Asha and "Wish"

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:56.968
is inherently very much
like that, as well.

00:05:56.968 --> 00:05:59.834
So, hopefully, your oldest
is going to enjoy it, too.

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:02.033
-Yeah.

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:05.667
-No, it's exciting when --
There are other stories to tell,

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.033
which I think is a good thing.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:10.534
Like, I think what drew me
to "Wish" was the fact that,

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:14.033
like, you're watching
an unsuspecting girl

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:15.501
step into a leadership role.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.501
It's not like
she was looking for it.

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:19.567
She just became it.

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:22.834
And she tries, she fails,
she tries again.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:24.400
Like, those are beautiful things

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.968
that I think children
should learn.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:27.834
-And, now, is it true
that your karaoke song

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:30.000
is a Disney song?
-Yes.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.567
-What is it?

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:33.567
-"Colors of the Wind"
from "Pocahontas."

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.934
-Oh, wow.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:37.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, come on!

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.133
The Vanessa Williams
credit version is everything.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.834
-Wow.
-She said...

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:46.434
♪ Can you paint with all
the colors of the wind? ♪

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:47.801
So good. Like...

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:49.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:52.834
-I will be doing that
in the shower tomorrow!

00:06:52.834 --> 00:06:54.734
-Yes!
-I cannot wait.

00:06:54.734 --> 00:06:57.000
What a delight to have you here.
Thank you so much.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.567
You guys, that's Ariana DeBose.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.567 --> 00:07:01.868
"Wish" is in theaters nationwide
on November 22nd.

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:04.801
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Iman Vellani.

